# `not` sits between `and` and the comparison, so it is reachable only where
# an `and` operand is expected. An arithmetic operand comes from the
# multiplication level, six rungs tighter, and never reaches it: `1 + not
# true` has no expression after the `+`.
#
# Pinned for the same reason as a_comparison_refuses_a_bitwise_tail: a parser
# that read one binding-power table would admit `not` anywhere a prefix is
# allowed, and nothing else in the corpus says it may not appear here.
print "{1 + not true}"
